    <section id="faq" class="sec" style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.075)">
      <div class="sec-glow gl-top" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:84px 28px">
        <div style="font-size:11.5px;letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#b9a8ff;margin-bottom:14px">FAQ</div>
        <h2 style="font-size:clamp(30px,3.4vw,44px);letter-spacing:-.03em;margin:0 0 40px">Questions people actually ask.</h2>
        <div class="faq-list" style="border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.075)">
          <details class="faq-item" open style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.075);padding:20px 4px">
            <summary style="list-style:none;cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--font-heading);font-weight:800;font-size:17.5px;display:flex;gap:16px;align-items:center"><span class="faq-plus" style="color:#b9a8ff;font-size:20px;line-height:1;flex:none">+</span>Does it work on any streaming site?</summary>
            <div class="faq-body"><p style="margin:12px 0 0 32px;font-size:15px;color:rgba(244,242,248,.65)">On practically all of them. Detection reads the page title and the video player rather than a hardcoded list of domains, so new mirrors usually work the moment they go up. If one doesn't, you can still add the show by hand in the web app.</p></div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item" style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.075);padding:20px 4px">
            <summary style="list-style:none;cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--font-heading);font-weight:800;font-size:17.5px;display:flex;gap:16px;align-items:center"><span class="faq-plus" style="color:#b9a8ff;font-size:20px;line-height:1;flex:none">+</span>Where exactly is my data stored?</summary>
            <div class="faq-body"><p style="margin:12px 0 0 32px;font-size:15px;color:rgba(244,242,248,.65)">In your browser's local extension storage, on your machine. There is no OtakuList account and no backend to sync to. You can export the whole list as JSON any time, and deleting the extension deletes the data.</p></div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item" style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.075);padding:20px 4px">
            <summary style="list-style:none;cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--font-heading);font-weight:800;font-size:17.5px;display:flex;gap:16px;align-items:center"><span class="faq-plus" style="color:#b9a8ff;font-size:20px;line-height:1;flex:none">+</span>What happens if a site gets blocked?</summary>
            <div class="faq-body"><p style="margin:12px 0 0 32px;font-size:15px;color:rgba(244,242,248,.65)">Nothing happens to your list. Progress is stored against the show, not the site, so you open a different mirror and keep going from the episode you were on.</p></div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item" style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.075);padding:20px 4px">
            <summary style="list-style:none;cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--font-heading);font-weight:800;font-size:17.5px;display:flex;gap:16px;align-items:center"><span class="faq-plus" style="color:#b9a8ff;font-size:20px;line-height:1;flex:none">+</span>Will it interrupt me while watching?</summary>
            <div class="faq-body"><p style="margin:12px 0 0 32px;font-size:15px;color:rgba(244,242,248,.65)">Once per show, with a small corner card you can dismiss. After you confirm a series, every later episode is recorded silently, no overlay, no sound, nothing on top of the player.</p></div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item" style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.075);padding:20px 4px">
            <summary style="list-style:none;cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--font-heading);font-weight:800;font-size:17.5px;display:flex;gap:16px;align-items:center"><span class="faq-plus" style="color:#b9a8ff;font-size:20px;line-height:1;flex:none">+</span>Is it really free?</summary>
            <div class="faq-body"><p style="margin:12px 0 0 32px;font-size:15px;color:rgba(244,242,248,.65)">Free and open source under MIT. No paid tier, no ads, no data to sell. If you want to support it, star the repo or send a pull request.</p></div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
